// PARAM: --analysis interval
// Minimal reproducer from issue #113: n=5 makes "n < 2" false, so the
// "return 1" branch is provably unreachable. Before the reachability-lift
// fix, the dead branch's own #ret := 1 assignment transfer still produced
// a non-bottom #ret=[1,1] from an already-unreachable predecessor state,
// and the exit node's join widened the result to a=[1,500] instead of the
// exact a=[500,500]. Locks in the fixed, precise result -- flat, no
// procedure recursion, no --context flag. The recursive-factorial variant of
// this same pattern is 06-recursive_factorial_dead_branch_no_bottom_leak.vimp,
// which proves its results exactly under entry-state context sensitivity.
void f(n) {
  if (n < 2) {
    return 1
  } else {
    return n * 100
  }
}

void main() {
  a := f(5);
  __voblint_check(a == 500) // PROVED
}
